(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[7 1 "// PEP 734's interpreters (queue 230; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 230\"): several Interps in one process over"] [8 1 "// the one GIL, CPython 3.14.10's Python/crossinterp.c, Python/crossinterp_data_lookup.h, Python/crossinterp_exceptions.h"] [9 1 "// and Modules/_interpretersmodule.c ported. An interpreter's state is its *Interp, reached through current.Interp as"] [10 1 "// before; nothing here runs in a program that creates no interpreter, but the comparison in gil.take (interpSwitch) and"] [11 1 "// finTrack's owner. A session (_PyXI_Enter, _PyXI_Exit) runs on the calling goroutine under a new *Thread of the target"] [12 1 "// interpreter: one OS thread, two thread states, as CPython's."] [23 1 "// interpConfig is PyInterpreterConfig. gil: \"default\", \"shared\" or \"own\": pyi has the one GIL (the design's table), the"] [24 1 "// value is data."] [30 1 "// xiState is an Interp's state for interpreters: what CPython keeps in PyInterpreterState beyond the module table."] [38 32 "// __main__.__loader__ set (the first session)"] [39 32 "// threads started and not finished (_thread._count)"] [40 32 "// the heap types' getters (_PyXIData_RegisterClass)"] [41 32 "// sync_module's per-interpreter cache, by __main__'s file"] [43 27 "// _interpqueues' module state"] [44 27 "// _interpchannels' module state"] [47 1 "// interpRegs are the active interpreter's registers (the design's table): package variables the hot paths read, an"] [48 1 "// interpreter's own, swapped by interpSwitch."] [54 2 "// the module states a native module keeps in package variables: _asyncio's, _csv's, os.register_at_fork's"] [58 2 "// maxStrDigits: sys.set_int_max_str_digits' limit, each interpreter's own (interp->long_state; py-eval-1122)"] [65 25 "// the live interpreters, oldest first"] [67 2 "// xiEndHooks run when an interpreter ends (the queues' and the channels' items unbound)"] [71 1 "// interpSwitch makes in's registers the active ones."] [87 1 "// switchThread makes t the running thread on this goroutine (PyThreadState_Swap)."] [100 41 "// the main interpreter has its own GIL, as CPython's reports it"] [103 1 "// namedConfig is init_named_config."] [107 94 "// _PyInterpreterConfig_INIT"] [129 1 "// update is _PyInterpreterConfig_UpdateFromDict (all: _InitFromDict, every field required)."] [201 1 "// newSubInterp is Py_NewInterpreterFromConfig: init_interp_settings' checks, then a fresh Interp: its sys, importlib and"] [202 1 "// the rest fill in at its first import, its __main__ exists at once."] [213 2 "// the limit the configuration gives (-X int_max_str_digits, PYTHONINTMAXSTRDIGITS, else 4300), not the main interpreter's"] [214 2 "// current one (py-eval-1122: test_int's test_int_max_str_digits_is_per_interpreter)"] [222 32 "// a new __main__'s, as pylifecycle.c's add_main_module leaves it"] [229 1 "// end is Py_EndInterpreter: the non-daemon threads joined, atexit's functions run, the streams flushed; the interpreter"] [230 1 "// leaves the table and its items in the queues and channels are unbound."] [266 1 "// The moment of an interpreter handle's death (queue 553; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 553\"): a stdlib"] [267 1 "// interpreter (_interpreters.create(reqrefs=True)) ends when its last handle's __del__ drops its references (decref), and"] [268 1 "// its items in the queues and channels are unbound then, as reference counting does at `del interp`. pyi's moment at del"] [269 1 "// (finDeleted, queue 222) asks Go's collector within a budget of a tenth of the wall time; past it, while a subinterpreter"] [270 1 "// is held by handles, the deletion is owed (xiDeathOwed) and settled by one collection round before the next operation"] [271 1 "// whose answer depends on interpreters being alive: the queues' get, get_count, is_full and list_all, the channels'"] [272 1 "// recv, get_count, get_info, list_all and list_interpreters."] [275 1 "// xiHeldByHandles is whether a subinterpreter is alive with handles' references (refs > 0 under reqrefs)."] [285 1 "// xiSettleDeaths is the owed collection round (xiDeathOwed), at most once per owed deletion."] [303 1 "// isRunningMain is is_running_main: a thread runs __main__."] [306 1 "// the static exceptions (crossinterp_exceptions.h), made on first use: shared as CPython's static types are; pyi's"] [307 1 "// NotShareableError is shared too (CPython's heap type per interpreter), so `except` matches across a session"] [346 1 "// notShareable is set_notshareableerror with a cause."] [356 1 "// xiLookupFailure is _set_xid_lookup_failure."] [371 1 "// xiUnwrap is _PyXI_UnwrapNotShareableError: a NotShareableError's cause raised in its place."] [379 1 "// xiData is _PyXIData_t: the owner's id, new_object as a closure over a copy of the data, the release of what it binds."] [395 1 "// xiGetter is _PyXIData_getdata_t."] [400 1 "// xiLookup is lookup_getdata by the object's exact type."] [477 1 "// xiBufferViewType is _interpreters' XIBufferView: what a shared memoryview's obj shows."] [494 16 "// queue 249: the other interpreter's view holds no export of its own"] [499 1 "// xiGetBasic is _get_xidata."] [513 1 "// xiGetData is _PyObject_GetXIData; fallback: _PyXIDATA_FULL_FALLBACK."] [538 1 "// xiMainFile is _Py_GetMainfile: __main__.__file__, \"\" when none."] [548 1 "// xiPickleData is _PyPickle_GetXIData."] [569 1 "// xiMissingMainAttr is check_missing___main___attr."] [579 1 "// xiPickleLoads is _PyPickle_Loads: on a missing __main__ attribute, once more with a __main__ loaded from the original"] [580 1 "// file under a bogus name, cached per interpreter (ensure_isolated_main)."] [625 1 "// xiGlobalNames counts co's LOAD_GLOBALs (identify_unbound_names): in globals, in builtins, neither."] [644 1 "// xiVerifyStateless is _PyCode_VerifyStateless."] [659 1 "// xiVerifyFunction is _PyFunction_VerifyStateless."] [673 1 "// xiReturnsOnlyNone is _PyCode_ReturnsOnlyNone: no generator, each return's value the constant None."] [693 1 "// xiFunctionData is _PyFunction_GetXIData: only stateless functions; the code shared (marshal's copy would equal it),"] [694 1 "// a new function over the running __main__'s globals on the other side."] [718 1 "// xiScript is get_script_xidata (pure 0): the code of a function, a code object or a compiled text."] [761 1 "// xiExcInfo is _PyXI_excinfo."] [785 2 "// a traceback.TracebackException, formatted"] [814 1 "// format is _PyXI_excinfo_format, \"\" and false for None."] [836 1 "// asObject is _PyXI_excinfo_AsObject."] [864 1 "// apply is _PyXI_excinfo_Apply: exc of t with the snapshot's text."] [873 1 "// xiSession is _PyXI_session."] [880 1 "// xiEnter is _enter_session and _PyInterpreterState_SetRunningMain."] [895 3 "// init_importlib's part a new __main__ shows: its __loader__ is BuiltinImporter"] [908 1 "// exit is _exit_session."] [945 1 "// xiSharedNS is _create_sharedns and _fill_sharedns (no fallback)."] [955 3 "// _copy_string_obj_raw: the name as UTF-8 (PyUnicode_AsUTF8AndSize: a lone surrogate's UnicodeEncodeError)"] [975 1 "// xiCall is struct interp_call; xiRun is _run_in_interpreter."] [1005 3 "// a dict goes by pickle (no getter for it)"] [1020 1 "// wrapNotShareable is wrap_notshareable."] [1028 1 "// xiFailure is the override of a session's error: 0 uncaught, else its _PyXI_errcode's meaning."] [1036 1 "// xiApplyNotShareable is _PyXI_ApplyError's _PyXI_ERR_NOT_SHAREABLE."] [1045 1 "// xiRun runs a script (code) or a call in in, the updates applied to __main__ first: the result, the excinfo of an"] [1046 1 "// uncaught exception, or err raised directly."] [1112 2 "// the preserved result: a copy when the session switched interpreters"] [1164 1 "// xiProtect runs f with a Go panic as a SystemError, so that the session always exits."] [1196 1 "// interpID is _PyInterpreterState_ObjectToID."] [1231 1 "// resolveInterp is resolve_interp (every pyi interpreter is ready once made)."] [1600 1 "// ExtSubinterp is a legacy subinterpreter made through the C API (py-eval-1122: pyctypes' Py_NewInterpreter, for"] [1601 1 "// _testcapi's run_in_subinterp): the interpreter and the session the calling thread entered it with."] [1607 1 "// ExtNewInterpreter is Py_NewInterpreter: a legacy subinterpreter (whenceLegacyCAPI, the \"legacy\" config), entered by the"] [1608 1 "// calling thread, whose thread state is the new interpreter's until ExtEndInterpreter."] [1626 1 "// ExtEndInterpreter is Py_EndInterpreter: the session left (the thread back in the interpreter it came from), then the"] [1627 1 "// interpreter ended (its threads joined, its atexit functions run)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[76 22] [132 53] [153 28] [168 20] [182 22] [183 42] [216 36] [335 27] [373 20] [403 39] [432 58] [519 27] [520 31] [524 28] [540 65] [541 47] [606 25] [607 62] [696 31] [704 55] [732 24] [748 43] [777 49] [778 23] [782 23] [853 24] [897 52] [898 55] [899 31] [916 26] [934 53] [956 43] [989 28] [995 34] [999 27] [1000 41] [1004 28] [1006 45] [1049 28] [1051 32] [1092 44] [1098 47] [1116 38] [1128 24] [1167 20] [1175 20] [1176 23] [1186 28] [1200 27] [1225 27] [1238 34] [1245 33] [1287 44] [1301 33] [1353 78] [1416 30] [1425 27] [1445 24] [1463 30] [1468 29] [1550 30] [1581 45] [1586 40]]} (go/file "interpreters.go" :imports [


