;; PEP 734's interpreters (queue 230; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "Design: 230"): several Interps in one process over
;; the one GIL, CPython 3.14.10's Python/crossinterp.c, Python/crossinterp_data_lookup.h, Python/crossinterp_exceptions.h
;; and Modules/_interpretersmodule.c ported. An interpreter's state is its *Interp, reached through current.Interp as
;; before; nothing here runs in a program that creates no interpreter, but the comparison in gil.take (interpSwitch) and
;; finTrack's owner. A session (_PyXI_Enter, _PyXI_Exit) runs on the calling goroutine under a new *Thread of the target
;; interpreter: one OS thread, two thread states, as CPython's.

